WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.215
Containment limits the spread or impact of an incident while the team continues to

00:00:04.215 --> 00:00:05.415
understand and resolve it.

00:00:05.415 --> 00:00:08.330
Containment can be narrow or broad depending on risk and confidence.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.930
Conceptually, it may involve isolating affected systems, disabling accounts,

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.909
restricting access, blocking traffic, pausing a workflow,

00:00:14.909 --> 00:00:17.660
rotating credentials, or applying temporary controls.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.699
The important point is that containment is a decision with tradeoffs.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:22.760
Acting too slowly can allow harm to grow.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.100
Acting too broadly can disrupt operations, interrupt customers,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.415
or remove evidence that analysts still need.

00:00:28.415 --> 00:00:32.150
Good containment is therefore coordinated with incident leadership, system owners,

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.450
business owners, and legal or privacy stakeholders when appropriate.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.480
Responders should ask what the action protects, what it might break,

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.215
what evidence must be preserved first,

00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:42.780
and how the action will be reversed or adjusted later.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.920
Temporary controls can buy time for deeper analysis and eradication.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.430
Every containment decision should leave a record: what was done, who approved it,

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:50.180
when it happened,

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.360
what risk it addressed, and what follow-up remains.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.940
Containment plans should include both the immediate action and the exit path.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.000
If an account is disabled, how will legitimate work continue?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.740
If a host is isolated, who validates it can return?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.780
If traffic is blocked, what monitoring confirms the block is helping?

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.080
These questions make containment safer and easier to explain.
